## Built from source

### Docker Agent

    Upstream:   https://github.com/docker/docker-agent
    Commit:     1a0e7ffbcbad4b2cbdd690f48689e87fb0c69599  (tag v1.128.0)
    Licence:    Apache-2.0
    Our image:  agentry-docker-agent-src
    Context:    build/docker-agent/

Copyright the Docker Agent authors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version
2.0; a copy is at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Upstream carries no
`NOTICE` file, so there are no additional attribution terms to relay.

**Changes we make** (Apache-2.0 §4(b) requires that modified files carry a
statement of the changes; `build/docker-agent/Dockerfile` states them in full):

1. Every base image resolves from our own registry by digest rather than a
   mutable public tag.
2. Upstream's floating `COPY --from=docker/mcp-gateway:v2` becomes a
   digest-pinned copy.
3. `DOCKER_AGENT_DISABLE_DESKTOP_PROXY=1` is set, closing the Docker Desktop PAC
   transport path that v1.127.0 attached to the unguarded transport the model
   clients use.
4. The cross-compilation stages (`tonistiigi/xx`, `crazymax/osxcross`, zig, and
   the darwin/windows paths) are dropped; this builds Linux only. The binary is
   still CGO with external linking and still asserted static.

Apache-2.0 §3 grants no trademark licence. Nothing built here may be presented
as a Docker product, and the name "Docker Agent" is used only to identify the
upstream component.

